4. PRIORITY P0 — ACCOUNT AND OAUTH ARCHITECTURE
==================================================

This is the highest priority.

Audit all platform connection, OAuth, credential and account-management code.

Support multiple independent accounts.

Platforms may include:
- YouTube
- Facebook
- Instagram
- TikTok
- Telegram
- Discord
- X
- LinkedIn
- Pinterest
- Other existing supported integrations.

Requirements:

A. Separate these concepts:

1. OAuth application credentials.
2. OAuth authorization grants.
3. Access and refresh tokens.
4. Connected platform accounts.
5. External account/channel IDs.
6. Publishing destinations.

Never treat them as the same thing.

B. Account isolation:

Every connected account must have a stable internal connection ID.

Every token must be associated with the correct provider, OAuth client and connection.

Never select an account using:
- Last connected account.
- Last saved credentials.
- Global active account.
- Platform name alone.
- An ambiguous fallback.

C. YouTube identity verification:

After OAuth connection:

1. Call the official YouTube API to identify the authenticated channel.
2. Retrieve the real channel ID.
3. Retrieve the actual channel title.
4. Store the external channel ID.
5. Compare it against existing connections.
6. Detect duplicate or conflicting mappings.
7. Show the verified channel identity in the UI.

If two records point to the same external channel ID, flag the conflict.

Do not pretend that two display names represent two independent YouTube channels.

Google OAuth grants can expose multiple Brand Account channels. Support this correctly rather than assuming every channel needs a separate token.

D. Disconnect and reconnect:

- Disconnect must affect only the selected connection.
- It must not delete other accounts.
- Reconnect must not overwrite unrelated credentials.
- Expired tokens must be handled safely.
- Invalid refresh tokens must show an actionable error.
- A token issued for another OAuth client must not silently be reused.

E. Facebook and Instagram:

Verify the real Page ID and Instagram professional account ID.

Handle official OAuth permission errors separately from network errors.

Do not claim a Facebook or Instagram account is connected until the actual account identity has been verified.

F. OAuth callbacks:

Verify that each configured callback is a real working backend route.

Do not assume GitHub Pages can act as an OAuth backend or callback relay by itself.

For HTTPS-only providers, use a properly configured HTTPS callback or secure tunnel/relay.

Acceptance tests:

- Connect account A.
- Connect account B.
- Verify A and B retain separate identities.
- Disconnect A.
- Confirm B remains connected.
- Reconnect A.
- Confirm B's credentials remain unchanged.
- Attempt to publish to A and verify the actual destination.
- Test duplicate external channel IDs.
- Test invalid and expired refresh tokens.

